      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found the issue that was impacting the canary backdrop filter tests. In `skia_renderer` there\u0027s a reverse-filter bounds call to detect when the backdrop filter \"moves\" pixels: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:components/viz/service/display/skia_renderer.cc;drc\u003d4af8f68bc5e5f94625410f60fc2506d7c8fd296f;l\u003d1493\n\nIf it doesn\u0027t move pixels, it doesn\u0027t add a `::Crop` filter to restrict the input that can be sampled. This lets backdrop color filters run on arbitrary canvas matrices, while adding a ::Crop forces a scale+translation decomposition that can have a visible impact on precise text that\u0027s not then blurred, etc.\n\nWith this CL, the value returned from the reverse-bounds query will always match the crop so the skia-renderer logic mis-identifies the backdrop filter as non-pixel moving and no longer adds the crop to the input. Without the crop element, the backdrop filter\u0027s source image is the entire page and the legacy crop bounds handling no longer clamps where it was meant to.\n\nI\u0027ll need to update skia-renderer\u0027s logic before this lands; it can definitely be cleaned up now with the new crop image filter factories. Good news is I don\u0027t think there\u0027s actually a logical issue with this change itself.",
      "parentUuid": "7318a90a_214cc048",
